Entrapment is a 1999 heist film directed by Jon
Amiel and written by Ronald Bass.

11
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
It stars Sean Connery and Catherine Zeta-Jones and includes
Will Patton, Ving Rhames and Maury Chaykin.

12
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The film focuses on the relationship between an investigator and a professional
thief as they attempt a heist at the turn of the millennium.

13
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
Simon West and Antoine Fuqua were both in talks
to direct before Amiel was hired.

14
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
Principal photography took place from June to October
1998 at locations in Britain and Malaysia.

15
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The score was composed by Christopher Young, and British singer
Seal performs "Lost My Faith" over the end credits.

16
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
Entrapment was released theatrically in the United States on 30
April 1999 and in the United Kingdom on 2 July.

17
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
It received mixed reviews from critics, and grossed $212 million
worldwide on a $66 million production budget.

18
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
The film explores themes of new year's eve, london,
england, distrust, undercover, burglar.

19
01:46:24,000 --> 01:46:30,000
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
